      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Dutzow, the first permanent German settlement in Missouri, was founded in 1832 by an immigrant from Lübeck, the 'Baron' Johann Wilhelm von Bock.",
